{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active","id":1555600,"title":"Infernals Backerkit campaign now active","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-18T12:30:49-08:00","id":1555600,"title":"Infernals Backerkit campaign now active","content":"<a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects/onyx-path/deluxe-exalted-infernals\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.backerkit.com/c/projects...lted-infernals</a><br /> <br /> It's not even been two hours and it's doubled its goal.<br /> <br /> Looking at the first manuscript preview, I think there's a lot of stuff in the works that will satisfy some people who had their doubts.<br /> <br /> It all arises from a key point: the Green Sun Princes aren't the Chosen of the Yozis, or even of the demons. They are the Chosen of <i>Hell</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T13:16:47-08:00","id":1555643,"title":"","content":"I'm very happy to say it's satisfied many of my doubts-if not all, then more than enough to await the rest of the content with hope rather than dread. I particularly enjoy the Carceral War and it's consequences for demonic society, the elaboration on what warlocks (even non-Infernal ones) actually are, the attempt to distinguish Hell as a freer and more unstable place than Yu-Shan and the defined but distant guidelines for Yozi interaction. I am greatly relieved the entire revolutionary/righteous indignation angle has been utterly de-emphasised in favour of revenge for it's own sake.<br /> <br /> This comes with the caveat that it has satisfied my doubts by being functionally unrecognisable to almost ANY information I could find about Infernals development in the years leading up to this; ironically it most reminds me of the initial preview for Infernals (the one with Basphomy in Verdigris) but less railroad-y (this is a good thing). <br /> <br /> It also comes with the caveat that while I am ALL FOR the very decisive pitch that Infernals are not, in fact, just Green Solars and nothing else. The reveal of what they actually are is such a lawyer-like way of saying &quot;Yes they are the Chosen of the Yozis but not of any SINGLE Yozi&quot; that I wish it had been advertised more strongly, and that in general the slant of Infernal &quot;humanism&quot; wasn't emphasised so much. A lot of my complaints would have been happily discarded if I knew THIS was what they were going for. Above all else I very much appreciate the hints there is more to embodying Hell than simply Charms as RAW. As I said in the other thread, I am more than happy to accept some other kind of inhuman transcendence even if it's not strictly Devil-Tigerhood as long as there IS one. And there seems to be one here.<br /> <br /> Even if nothing is set in stone, from the first draft alone I am much, much, <b>MUCH </b>more willing to give 3e Infernals the benefit of the doubt than I was based on any and all promotional information between this and the very first preview.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T20:03:23-08:00","id":1555659,"title":"","content":"Was there some kind of &quot;Infernal humanism&quot; pitched? Because it doesn't seem like a thing that showed up in Essence where Infernal Charms were concerned. They're all about freaking the mundanes with how monstrous you are, covering yourself with demonic verdigris, and irradiating plot-important objects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-19T21:27:29-08:00","id":1555663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1555659#post1555659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there some kind of &quot;Infernal humanism&quot; pitched? Because it doesn't seem like a thing that showed up in Essence where Infernal Charms were concerned. They're all about freaking the mundanes with how monstrous you are, covering yourself with demonic verdigris, and irradiating plot-important objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was pushed the most early on, but both from what what others said and what the devs told me on Discord it was HEAVILY pushed as the new slant for Infernals with a de-emphasis on the Yozis and Hell. It is a testament to how misleading the commentary given about Infernals was that I was concerned Infernals would be roughly as alien as Abyssals before seeing the current draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T02:11:52-08:00","id":1555678,"title":"","content":"I disagree on the perspective of things leading up to this point, but I think that should be confined as a bygone from hereon in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-20T11:05:58-08:00","id":1555688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Organ Boy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1555663#post1555663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was pushed the most early on, but both from what what others said and what the devs told me on Discord it was HEAVILY pushed as the new slant for Infernals with a de-emphasis on the Yozis and Hell. It is a testament to how misleading the commentary given about Infernals was that I was concerned Infernals would be roughly as alien as Abyssals before seeing the current draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernals are still not using the literal Charms that Yozis have, and the Yozis have been pushed back, with more emphasis put on their souls and them as distant things that you can't really just talk to. They still interact with humans through mostly the emotions they get in humans in spite and malice. And they still have less a theme of becoming not Infernal Exalted anymore and more touching on the cosmic as part of being that instead.<br /> <br /> Like, a lot of this TBH is you looking to read things as toxically and uncharitably as possible. And your going saying we were wrong when...it's still what hte devs have said and folks like me have tried to communicate doesn't do much to me to temper that imperession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude21","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T06:04:09-08:00","id":1555718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1555688#post1555688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernals are still not using the literal Charms that Yozis have, and the Yozis have been pushed back, with more emphasis put on their souls and them as distant things that you can't really just talk to. They still interact with humans through mostly the emotions they get in humans in spite and malice. And they still have less a theme of becoming not Infernal Exalted anymore and more touching on the cosmic as part of being that instead.<br /> <br /> Like, a lot of this TBH is you looking to read things as toxically and uncharitably as possible. And your going saying we were wrong when...it's still what hte devs have said and folks like me have tried to communicate doesn't do much to me to temper that imperession.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't read things as &quot;toxic&quot; and &quot;uncharitable&quot; if instead of repeatedly emphasising the idea that Infernals would somehow be using <i>less </i>Yozi power they would be using <i>more </i>Yozi power as is my reading of the current drafts. I refuse to accept any blame when all parties other than myself who purported to know more about the game's development gave the impression of a completely different outcome while dismissing all my concerns, and in some cases outright blaming me for liking the old material.<br /> <br /> All anyone had to do was actually <i>quantify </i>what being &quot;the Chosen of Hell&quot; actually entailed instead of letting it stand as this nebulous abstraction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T06:11:08-08:00","id":1555721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1555678#post1555678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree on the perspective of things leading up to this point, but I think that should be confined as a bygone from hereon in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on how you've comported yourself, I have no reason to accept any kind of value judgement from you at face value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26460-organ-boy","name":"Organ Boy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-21T10:22:09-08:00","id":1555728,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">I've been summoned by reports to this thread, which I can only assume due to an utter lack of context, is a result of prior arguments from another thread being dragged here. Don't do that. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T03:32:13-08:00","id":1555750,"title":"","content":"So, I certainly liked ExEss Infernals, and how they made you feel demonic without having to be a cackling villain (and the emphasis on righteous indignation makes sense for a mixed exalts game), but I was also quietly keeping the Devil-Tiger stuff as one possible end-point of your Devil-Body evolving, and I always assumed they could still be jerks.<br /> <br /> What I've seen of Ex3 Infernals so far looks really good, and is rightly broader than the version we saw in ExEss. They feel hellish, powerful, and as capable of being evil as they were before. This book has also come at the right time, since I'm about to start an Ex3 game.<br /> <br /> Frankly, this is getting me excited about the full game again! I'd almost written it off for Essence, but this makes me want to play again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T10:11:14-08:00","id":1555758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1555750#post1555750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as capable of being evil as they were before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think &quot;take vengeance on the Yozis' behalf, with them as your enthusiastic (verging on loving) tutors in that&quot; offers a lot more scope for that than &quot;do stuff which will make Creation more closely resemble Hell, which will in some way help&quot;.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, it's a lot easier to reconcile with the Green Sun Princes pursuing their own ambitions, and can sustain a more long term relationship with the Demon Realm.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-07T23:31:04-08:00","id":1556334,"title":"","content":"So all the charms are out and honestly, they are very well done even with some of the (very fitting )gaps in competency.<br /> <br /> I still am enjoying these.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T10:06:23-08:00","id":1556346,"title":"","content":"I've only read through Awareness thus far, but I find it very compelling to answer my longstanding question of how complicated the variety of influences should be as &quot;yes, fuck you&quot;, and that the cohesive through line of Abilities seems to be &quot;pile in as much weird shit there as even vaguely attaches to the core capability&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like, it's a lot, but it works, because it's neat to have such variety of weird manifestations and applications while still feeling grounded in the human actions (and persona for stuff running on Intimacies) at the core of it. You get pinnacles that feel like they express awe-inspiring might or world-building authority, at the same time as there's apparent trade off for being extremely good in a direct way that the Solars have.<br /> <br /> I'm personally not really here for transhumanism as a framing, but I do like that there's transformative stuff like becoming weirdly big or having a freaky appetite.<br /> <br /> And I do think it has threaded the needle of making the Yozis (and other forces) apparent while the dispersal makes it feel less like direct expression of them.<br /> <br /> I also like how the Universal Charms feel like useful and consequential refinement of the core Infernal being while not stepping on the Abilities or feeling strictly necessary. Like, they're useful but not so useful that they demand investment. Devil-Body enhancement stands out especially there; it's nice to have options to increase the powers, add alternate forms for it, and increase the pace of access, but it never fully departs from the point that the transformation is something that happens under duress and doesn't quite sit comfortably on the Exalt. Hence, that limited access makes it feel completely suitable to not really invest in it compared to more direct stuff.<br /> <br /> I actually have this character concept of an Infernal who not only neglects enhancing their Devil-Body, but dislikes it and actively tries to avoid using it. Not because of anything to do with departure from humanity, but regarding it as something undignified and humiliating for the transformation conditions. A manifestation of desperation that withdraws from the self-realisation of the Exalt for a shell of crude Hellish power, far less impressive than their deliberately cultivated and exerted capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-08T16:07:49-08:00","id":1556372,"title":"","content":"The main question in my mind is whether any Yozi's themes are at least theoretically valid design space for any Ability. I mean, you wouldn't want to just copy Hegra-themed Archery Charms into Melee or whatever, but plausibly you could have colorful emotion-related sword techniques of some kind?<br /> <br /> Of course, Infernal Charms need to generally have that Hellish twist -- otherwise they'd just be green Solars and we wouldn't need a new book -- but Hell can twist in a lot of different directions.<br /> <br /> There does seem to be a lot of variation into how much different Charms <i>require</i> the Infernal to play into their themes -- some are pretty solid even if you aren't doing anything special, like Hellbound Mariner Saga (which has a key that makes it work to full effect all the time), and some are greatly nerfed if you aren't doing the Hell thing, like Foremost Vengeance Stratagem (whose keys all rely on fulfilling its conditions).<br /> <br /> TBH, it seems like not only the Yozis themselves but also demons can be evoked in some cases -- Sable Revelry Summons is clearly based on Erembour more than the Ebon Dragon himself, and Demon-Legion Emulation evokes various First Circle demons. The possibilities seem nearly limitless.<br /> <br /> There have been a few Charms that don't seem very impressive for Solar-tier Exalted -- Sermon of the Yozis seems <i>painfully</i> overspecialized -- but overall I've really been enjoying this stuff. If only there were a few more Charms for doing sorcerous workings more effectively...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T04:57:21-08:00","id":1556379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1555600-infernals-backerkit-campaign-now-active?p=1556372#post1556372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, you wouldn't want to just copy Hegra-themed Archery Charms into Melee or whatever, but plausibly you could have colorful emotion-related sword techniques of some kind?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it needs to be something that draws upon the element where Hegra isn't just a force of emotions, but one of Hell's primary weather systems. Shooting arrows has that whole wind association which provides the hook.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say exclude the Yozi altogether, just that it might not have much depth or breadth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-09T08:15:31-08:00","id":1556381,"title":"","content":"I can't count the number of games and anime where someone does stuff with the air by swinging their sword very hard or very skillfully -- although this might admittedly be hard to scale up to the &quot;shoot a city-killing storm cloud into the sky&quot; level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T11:59:24-08:00","id":1556805,"title":"","content":"I believe that the campaign would be over now, with it having raised enough to get all but the very last minute added stretch goal (which was just the fourth round of adding Charms for the companion book anyway).<br /> <br /> I for one am happy that we hit the goal to get some more focus on warlocks, including the extra Eclipse Charms to equip them with. I actually upped my own pledge by a couple hundred to help get to that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}